# What the application image must not carry.
#
# The build context is the repository root, so without this file every build
# would upload node_modules, the client's build output and the git history to
# the daemon -- hundreds of megabytes per build, for files the image rebuilds or
# does not use at all.

# Reinstalled in the image from the lockfile, so what is on the host is
# irrelevant -- and a Windows or macOS node_modules is not just useless here, it
# is wrong (native binaries for the wrong platform).
node_modules
**/node_modules

# `next build` runs inside the image.
client/.next
client/out

# Real secrets. No image should contain one, and `.env.local` is where the
# client keeps a developer's.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env.local
!**/.env.local.example

# The database image's recipe now lives in docker-compose.yml, so this context
# has no docker/ directory to exclude.

# Nothing in an image reads these.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
docs

# The suites need a live database and are never run from the image. If you want
# `docker compose run --rm api npm test`, delete the next two lines.
**/test
**/tests

# Editor and OS noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
